# Documentation (docs/)

When adding or updating code, create or update the corresponding documentation.

## Scope

- New or changed compiler/IDE behavior → update or add a doc under `docs/` (e.g. COMPILER-PIPELINE.md, PREPROCESSOR.md).
- New built-ins or runtime → see `docs/ADDING-A-BUILTIN.md` and relevant topic docs (e.g. BUILTIN-FUNCTIONS.md, ARCHITECTURE-C.md).
- High-level index: `docs/INDEX.md`, `docs/README.md`.

## Style

- Use clear headings and short paragraphs.
- Prefer concrete examples and code snippets.
- Keep filenames UPPERCASE with hyphens (e.g. `COMPILER-PIPELINE.md`).
- For pipeline/architecture, a single diagram plus bullet summary is often enough; see COMPILER-PIPELINE.md.

## Cross-links

Link between related docs (e.g. from INDEX or README to specific topic files) rather than duplicating long sections.
